ular part of the rectangle. The vertices of this triangle are \\((0, 0)\\), \\((3, 4)\\), and \\((3, 0)\\).\n\nThe area of the rectangle is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the rectangle} = (3 - (-7))(4 - (-1)) = 10 \\times 5 = 50.\n\\]\n\nThe area of the triangle where \\(a > b\\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the triangle} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 4 = 20.\n\\]\n\nThe probability that a randomly chosen point \\((a, b)\\) from the rectangle lies in the triangle where \\(a > b\\) is the ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the rectangle:\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Area of the triangle}}{\\text{Area of the rectangle}} = \\frac{20}{50} = \\frac{2}{5}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability that \\(\\log_{2}(a - b)\\) is defined is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{2}{5}}.\n\\]\n\nLet \\( D \\) be the determinant of the matrix with column vectors \\( u \\), \\( ev \\), and \\(gv \\), where\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} u \\\\ v \\\\ g \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad u + v + g = 2.\n\\]\nCompute the minimum value of the determinant function \\( z(u,v,g) = \\text{det} \\left [ \\begin{array}{ccc} u & v & g \\ \\\\ ev & gv & 0 \\\\ gv & 0 & 1 \\end{array} \\right]. \\)\n\nTo compute the determinant of the matrix\n\\[\nA = \\begin{pmatrix} u & v & g \\\\ ev & gv & 0 \\\\ gv & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\nwe expand the determinant along the third column, which contains a single non-zero entry. The determinant of \\(A\\) is given by\n\\[\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot \\det \\begin{pmatrix} ev & gv \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} - 0 \\cdot \\det \\begin{pmatrix} u & v \\\\ gv & 1 \\end{pmatrix} + 0 \\cdot \\det \\begin{pmatrix} u & v \\\\ ev & gv \\end{pmatrix} = ev \\cdot 1 - gv \\cdot 0 = ev.\n\\]\nThus, the determinant of \\(A\\) is\n\\[\n\\det(A) = ev.\n\\]\nNext, we need to find the possible values of \\(e\\) and \\(v\\) given the condition \\(u + v + g = 2\\). The vectors \\(u\\), \\(v\\), and 